WEBVTT

00:31:55.451 --> 00:32:01.337
Bess: Ummm ... I have no ...
I have no idea.

00:32:02.200 --> 00:32:05.122
Jessica: Well, is there a thing
that you regularly go back to,

00:32:05.146 --> 00:32:07.959
like when it's cold and you're bummed,
and you just need ...

00:32:07.983 --> 00:32:10.366
AG: So how do you create
a rapid connection?

00:32:10.390 --> 00:32:12.456
Here's what Jane Dutton is listening for.

00:32:12.480 --> 00:32:14.567
JD: What is the first move that was made?

00:32:14.591 --> 00:32:16.336
What was the first question?

00:32:16.360 --> 00:32:20.276
Did they go to something
that's sort of routine,

00:32:20.300 --> 00:32:22.182
like, you know, "Where'd you grow up?"

00:32:22.206 --> 00:32:27.238
or do they go to a question
that really communicates deep interest

00:32:27.262 --> 00:32:29.496
and kind of positive regard for another,

00:32:29.520 --> 00:32:34.316
like, "What is the most meaningful
thing that happened to you this week?"